    "source": "default",
    "doc": "'local' (default): a claim is an event in this clone's log, so two offline clones can both claim one item (detected afterwards as 'contested'). 'remote': a claim also creates refs/ddflow/claims/<id> on `remote` by compare-and-swap, so only one clone wins while online; release, complete and expiry delete it and a heartbeat extends it. A refused claim names the holder; an unreachable remote refuses the claim (never silently local). An unrecognised value in a config file is warned about, reported by `doctor` and falls back to 'local', the strictest (a typo never writes claim refs to the remote; claims stay in this clone); `config --set`, `ddflow_configure` and the environment refuse it, and so does loading ddflow's own source tree, where the file and the code are one commit."
