    "doc": "Whether `tools/list` declares an `outputSchema` for every tool whose result is a JSON object of declared fields (not `show`, `decision_show` or `recall`, which answer one record or null, nor text), and a call returns that object also as `structuredContent` (not when it failed; MCP 2025-06-18 and later; an older client is served as with `off`). `off` (default): the result is the JSON text in the first content block only, and `tools/list` is as small as before. `on`: each object tool lists `{\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"schema\": {\"const\": \"<tool>@<n>\"}, <its declared fields>: {}}}` -- additive, nothing required -- and a bare-array tool lists its schema under `_meta[\"ddflow/outputSchema\"]`, since an `outputSchema` must be an object. Costs about 16 KB more `tools/list` and every object result is sent twice (the text block and `structuredContent`). Every object result carries its `schema` tag either way. Read once at server start, so change it and restart the server. An unrecognised value in a config file is warned about, reported by `doctor` and falls back to 'off', the strictest (no safety dimension; the smaller, unchanged tool list and result); `config --set`, `ddflow_configure` and the environment refuse it, and so does loading ddflow's own source tree, where the file and the code are one commit."
